import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.PathVariable;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/billing")
public class InvoiceController {

    private final InvoiceService invoiceService;

    public InvoiceController(InvoiceService invoiceService) {
        this.invoiceService = invoiceService;
    }

    @GetMapping("/invoices/{id}")
    public ResponseEntity<ApiResponse<?>> getInvoice(@PathVariable long id) {
        var invoice = invoiceService.getInvoice(id);
        return ResponseEntity.ok(ApiResponse.ok(invoice));
    }
}
```

Notes:
- Single GET endpoint, constructor injection, response wrapped in `ApiResponse.ok(...)` per convention — no pagination needed since it's a single-resource lookup, and no try/catch: if `getInvoice` throws a domain exception for a missing invoice (e.g. `InvoiceNotFoundException`), it's expected to be handled by the existing `@RestControllerAdvice`.
- `ApiResponse` is assumed to already exist as a shared type (as in the skill's examples); swap the import path if your project places it elsewhere.

